{"type":"text","timestamp":1787412620655,"sessionID":"ses_fd5ea5379ffeljFyMS5ZkLq4V9","part":{"id":"prt_02a1817de001gbuGpfICTwcnmi","messageID":"msg_02a180bfc001Hdqa1WPMOPaVCv","sessionID":"ses_fd5ea5379ffeljFyMS5ZkLq4V9","type":"text","text":"All requirements are met. Summary of the change to `lib/glob-match.js`:\n\n- Added `stripCallbacks` to drop `ignore`/`onResult`/`onMatch`/`onIgnore` from options before building sub/ignore matchers (so the ignore pattern never inherits the caller's callbacks).\n- Built an `ignoreMatcher` from `opts.ignore` (a glob or array of globs).\n- In the single-pattern `matcher`: after testing the pattern, if it matched but the ignore matcher also matches, the input is `ignored` and the final decision is non-match. The result object carries `glob`, `regex`, `input`, `output`, `isMatch` (final decision) plus existing fields. `onResult` fires once per input; `onMatch` only when it matches; `onIgnore` only when excluded by ignore. Inputs that never matched the pattern are reported as non-match, never ignored.\n- Extended the array matcher similarly (sub-matchers stripped of callbacks; ignore + callbacks applied once at the array level), preserving existing boolean return behavior.\n\nExisting behavior (array patterns, `returnObject` form, boolean results) is unchanged, and the pre-existing test failures are baseline (present before my change).","time":{"start":1787412617182,"end":1787412620645}}}
